 lines=['# Four-bar numerical constraint-fidelity audit','','Machine: easteregg2. This is a pinned-hip fixture with the source geometry, all source body mass/inertia arrays, lever arms, and hinge damping preserved. All robot degrees of freedom except three knee hinges are pinned explicitly; no muscles, SNS, BPA, footcontact, or robotstandingtrial is involved. The external fixture holds its single anatomical knee coordinate using documented gravity/load feedforward and a50ms critically damped servo. That fixture apparatus is not a robotcontroller.','','## Source accounting and gaps','','Each connectconstraint has rank2 across the three planar hinges. Static solutions balance gravity and knownnativeback-hinge torques with forward/inverse and equation-of-motion errors at floatingpointprecision. Sourcegravity-only gaps are0.498mm right and0.522mm left; signed8–9Nm back-hinge loads produce approximately7.53–9.76mm gaps. All appliedload, holdingactuator, and actualconstraint torques are logged separately. The stronger closed-reference normaljointcouple also logs its point-force equivalent, which is not silently treated as a dynamically reapplied pointload.','','| Side | Knownback load Nm | Sourcegap mm | Numericalvariant gap µm |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
